  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Slot operation gets two new parameters (issue 1731, maintainer request: \"the slot operation should be possible to extend outside the face or edge selected in the direction of its length\"):\n\n- `extend_start`: how far the pass runs past A, along B to A, in mm.\n- `extend_end`: how far the pass runs past B, along A to B, in mm.\n\nBoth are zero by default. The command refuses a negative or a non-finite value at creation.\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/slot_ends.rs` (new): `slot_extended_ends` moves the two endpoints along the slot direction. The generator `slot()` does not change.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: the Slot arm cuts between the extended ends. The pick room law (#1504) still judges the authored slot.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/material_source.rs`: the Slot's machine area is the stadium of the extended ends.\n- The part laws do not change. On a part source, the part section judges the extended pass. On a stock source, the setup's parts judge it (#1607). An extension into a kept part is a blocking Gouge, and the post refuses the program.\n- Project file: the DTO writes the keys only when they are not zero. The parameter digest appends them only when one is not zero. Earlier slots keep their file text, stamp and output.\n- MCP: `edit_operation` reaches the fields through the Slot DTO merge patch.\n- UI: two rows, \"Extend past A\" and \"Extend past B\", on the Slot Geometry tab, below \"Slot width\". The layout of the other fields does not change (issue 1732 is for that layout).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1731-slot-end-extension.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/slot_extension.rs`:\n\n- `the_pass_extends_by_the_given_distance_at_each_end`: the feed span goes from x -15..15 to x -20..23 for 5 mm / 8 mm. The path is clean and posts.\n- `an_extension_into_the_part_is_a_gouge_and_never_posts`: on a part source, the authored slot is clean. An extension of 5 mm at either end into the channel wall is a blocking Gouge, and `post_setup` refuses.\n- `off_the_stock_an_extension_into_a_kept_part_is_a_gouge`: the same result on a stock source with the part in the setup.\n- `the_extensions_ride_the_command_undo_the_file_and_the_stamp`: refusal of bad values, `EditOperationParams` and undo, save and load, no keys at zero, stamp changes only when set.\n- `mcp_edit_operation_reaches_the_slot_extensions`: MCP patch is taken; a negative value is refused.\n\nUnit tests in `slot_ends.rs`: zero is the authored slot, the direction, and the refusals.\n\nTargeted suites run green: motion lib `slot_ends`; app `slot_extension`, `slot_caps`, `slot_picks`, `slot_pick_refusals`, `project_roundtrip`, `golden_cl`, `operations`, `mcp`, `stock_source_law`, `kept_parts_live`, `refusal_ghost`, `solid_law_goldens`, `cutting_data`, `tool_cutting_rows`, `microarc_test_part`, `index_swing`, `index_swing_horizontal`, `fourth_axis_pose`, `rotary_subplate`, `rotary_subplate_standing`, `pocket_recognition`, `recorded_post_streams`; ui lib. Clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-motion, camcraft-app and camcraft-ui (all targets) is clean. No golden or snapshot changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick tier: its plan selects almost every suite (the gate maps name `app::operation` and `motion::machining2d`). Only the suites above ran.\n- An extension on a Selection (picked) source. The code path is the same as on a part source, but no test picks a face.\n- No screenshots: this worker cannot start the GUI. The UI change is two number rows on the Slot Geometry tab.\n- The Trochoidal slot does not get the extension.\n\nChangelog: Slot: new \"Extend past A\" and \"Extend past B\" parameters run the pass past each end along the slot; an extension into a kept part is refused as a gouge.\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1731\n",
